{"Bulgarian_Infantry(axis_minor)" "Bulgarian line infantry armed predominantly with bolt‑action rifles. Reliable for holding ground and steady advances; benefits from attached machine‑gun or mortar support in offence."}
{"hungarian_smg_squad(axis_minor)" "Hungarian close‑quarters squad mixing Danuvia 39M and captured PPSh‑41 SMGs. Built for assaults in streets and trenches"}
{"romanian_rifle_squad(axis_minor)" "Romanian rifle section with an integral light machine‑gun team. Provides a balanced base of fire for defense and supports advances with suppressive LMG bursts."}
{"fin_pioneer(axis_minor)" "Finnish assault pioneers combining a flamethrower, light machine‑gun, SMGs and riflemen with demo tools. Suited for breaching bunkers and clearing trenches. Can dig trenches."}
{"Motorized_Hungarian_Rifles(axis_minor)" "Truck‑borne Hungarian rifle squad blending SMGs and rifles with an LMG element. Ideal for fast flanking and objective grabs."}
{"fin_kaukopartio(axis_minor)" "Finnish long‑range patrol (Kaukopartio) for deep raids and ambush. SMGs, rifles, and an LMG team to fix or break contact. Elevated stamina supports long movements and quick disengagements."}
{"Bersaglieri(axis_minor)" "Italian Bersaglieri with mixed rifles, SMGs, and a Breda LMG team. Agile in mobile firefights."}
{"Sissi(axis_minor)" "Finnish ‘Sissi’ light troops skilled in reconnaissance and guerrilla tactics. Compact LMG element supports SMG rushes and rifle fire."}
{"Hungarian_Assualt_Infantry(axis_minor)" "Heavily armed assault group with massed SMGs, an LMG team, Panzerfausts, and a flamethrower. Built for trench breaches and room‑to‑room fighting. High stamina on assault elements enables sustained pushes."}
{"Alpini(axis_minor)" "Italian Alpini mountain troops with rifles, SMGs, a Breda LMG team, and a marksman. Effective in rough terrain. Marksman elements show solid stamina for climbs and relocations."}
{"Bersaglieri_Mot(axis_minor)" "Motorized Bersaglieri section mixing rifles, SMGs, and LMG support. Ideal for quick redeployments and flanking."}
{"Paracadutisti(axis_minor)" "Italian Paracadutisti with dual LMGs, SMGs and rifles for sustained assaults. Airborne elements exhibit higher stamina for extended actions."}
{"tankcrew(axis_minor)" "Five‑man Hungarian tank crew intended to man vehicles and field guns. Poor infantry skirmishers; use to re‑crew valuable equipment. Slightly slower on foot than line infantry."}
{"vet_tankcrew(axis_minor)" "Veteran single tank crewman for rapid re‑crewing of vehicles or guns. Limited personal firepower. Slightly slower on foot than line infantry."}
{"sappers(axis_minor)" "Romanian mine‑disposal pair trained to detect and clear enemy minefields. Can dig trenches. Vulnerable while working."}
{"vehic_supporter(axis_minor)" "Bulgarian 2‑man support crew for vehicles and weapon emplacements. Minimal small‑arms capability."}
{"carcano(axis_minor)" "Single Italian rifleman with Carcano—picket duty and point defense."}
{"zb_24rifle(axis_minor)" "Single Romanian rifleman with ZB‑24—screening and security."}
{"orita(axis_minor)" "Single Romanian Orita SMG gunner—close‑quarters point defense."}
{"suomi_m31(axis_minor)" "Single Finnish Suomi KP/‑31 gunner—excellent CQB volume of fire; ideal for room entry and trench clearing."}
{"danuvia(axis_minor)" "Single Hungarian Danuvia SMG gunner—fast, compact CQB support."}
{"AP_Miners(axis_minor)" "Four Bulgarian sappers to lay anti‑personnel mines and wire. Create minefields to deny routes and fix infantry before assaults."}
{"AT_Miners(axis_minor)" "Four Bulgarian sappers with anti‑tank mines and hedgehogs. Emplace obstacles to canalize armor into AT kill zones."}
{"solothurn_31m(axis_minor)" "Two‑man Hungarian light MG team (Solothurn 31M). Provides mobile suppressive fire to pin enemies and cover maneuvers."}
{"zb_vz26(axis_minor)" "Two‑man Bulgarian ZB vz. 26 LMG team—compact base‑of‑fire element for bunker entry support and hasty assaults."}
{"breda30_alpini(axis_minor)" "Two‑man Alpini Breda 30 LMG team—steady suppressive fire for clearing small positions."}
{"breda30_bers(axis_minor)" "Two‑man Bersaglieri Breda 30 LMG team—mobile suppressive fire to force movement from cover."}
{"breda30_para(axis_minor)" "Two‑man paratrooper Breda 30 LMG team—airborne base‑of‑fire; coordinate with rifle elements for obscuration."}
{"Boys_AT_Rifle(axis_minor)" "Finnish two‑man Boys anti‑tank rifle team—effective vs. light armor and soft‑skins; finish disabled vehicles or clear exposed crews."}
{"pzb_at_Rifle(axis_minor)" "Bulgarian two‑man anti‑tank rifle team (PzB)—ambush light vehicles and harass transports; close to finish when crews are exposed."}
{"panzerfaust(axis_minor)" "Two Hungarian Panzerfaust operators—disposable close‑range anti‑armor punch; use cover and angles to approach armor. Assault elements demonstrate strong stamina for closing to range."}
